# ─── Docker build context ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The two images need src/, config/, alembic/ and the requirement files. Everything
# here is either a different product (the Next.js app), a local artefact, or a
# secret — and without these lines the context is ~3 GB (.venv, web/node_modules,
# web/.next, docs PDFs, the SQLite scratch databases), which Render uploads on
# every build.

# ─── Secrets — never in an image, never in a build layer ─────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.secrets/
web/.env
web/.env.local
.vercel/
.vercel-tmp/
.mcp.json

# ─── The frontend (deployed separately, on Vercel) ───────────────────────────
web/

# ─── Local environments, caches, scratch ─────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.tools-cache/
scripts/
exports/
.coverage
*.db
*.sqlite3

# ─── Documentation and report material ──────────────────────────────────────
docs/
*.md

# ─── Not used by either image ────────────────────────────────────────────────
docker-compose.yml
render.yaml
pyproject.toml
